{"ts":"2026-08-29T15:17:13.352Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-5.6-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"4c3bbebc779deae6780a83dd","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-5.6-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"release-operator","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-7zs0","claim:pm-vwuidf","release:pm-ntnv4k"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-7zs0+pm-vwuidf","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-7zs0","claim:pm-vwuidf","release:pm-ntnv4k"]}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-s8cth5"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1154: linked-test sandbox guard is command-shape inconsistent and undocumented"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The linked-test add guard rejects direct node --test commands containing space-separated flags but accepts equivalent execution through sh -c, equals-spelled flags, or alternate runners. This makes the policy both bypassable and unnecessarily obstructive, while pm test help does not disclose content validation."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","area:test-command","regression","sandbox-safety","trust"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-29T15:17:13.352Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-29T15:17:13.352Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Define whether the linked-test add policy is a security boundary or an agent-safety nudge and encode that contract in the public SDK.; Normalize or safely inspect direct, sh -c, equals-spelled, package-manager, Node, and non-Node runner forms so equivalent capabilities cannot diverge accidentally.; Document command-content validation and safe recovery in pm test help and testing documentation.; Add negative and positive regression tests with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage and manual temporary-workspace acceptance."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/definition_of_ready","value":"Read the complete pm-q813, pm-mlc3, and pm-ed28wi lineage plus the current src/cli/commands/test.ts and public SDK trust contracts before choosing the enforcement model."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"project management = context management"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Make linked-test safety classification capability-aware, consistent across equivalent command forms, and discoverable before mutation."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Agents can record precise acceptance tests without learning wrapper bypasses, while the intended workspace-data safety boundary remains enforceable and explainable."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"Removes a misleading shape-based guard that currently rewards less inspectable shell wrapping and surprises agents only after mutation."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"Equivalent linked-test executions receive equivalent safety classification, supported runners are intentionally defined, and pm test help documents the rule and safe recovery path."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"GitHub issue #1154 was reported during PR #1149 closeout and reproduces on published pm 2026.8.28; documenting it now prevents the finding from being lost or misclassified as already-completed trust work."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-n7rr"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"pm 2026.8.28 and 2026.8.21 on Linux/Node 24; linked-test mutation paths in CLI and SDK."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Run pm test ITEM --add-json with node --test x.ts and observe refusal; then add sh -c wrapping, an equals-spelled Node flag, node test/x.test.ts, or pytest -k and observe acceptance."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Commands with equivalent execution capability are classified consistently, the policy's security boundary is explicit, and help reveals all content constraints before mutation."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Direct node --test x.ts is refused while multiple equivalent or broader command forms are stored; the help contract does not mention command-content validation."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/affected_version","value":"2026.8.28"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"sdk/test-trust-and-cli-test-intake"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/regression","value":true},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/customer_impact","value":"Agents encounter a surprising refusal for the canonical Node test form and are nudged toward less inspectable wrappers that bypass the same guard."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-ed28wi","kind":"incident_from","created_at":"2026-08-29T15:17:13.352Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-q813","kind":"recurs_from","created_at":"2026-08-29T15:17:13.352Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-vwuidf","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-29T15:17:13.352Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-29T15:17:13.352Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Duplicate-check evidence: complete all-status keyword searches found closed pm-q813 for package-manager run-script wrappers, pm-mlc3 for package-manager flag prefixes, and pm-ed28wi for merge-time command provenance/trust. None owns capability-equivalent command normalization or missing pm test help disclosure. This issue recurs from pm-q813, is an incident in the broader trust boundary, and was discovered during pm-vwuidf exact-head closeout."}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-29T15:17:13.352Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"GitHub source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1154. Keep this item open and unclaimed until implementation is actively scheduled; PR #1149 only performs durable intake."}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/learnings","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-29T15:17:13.352Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"String-token deny rules are not execution-capability boundaries: accepting sh -c around a refused command makes the bypass less inspectable than the direct form and creates counterproductive agent UX."}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/escape_class","value":"production_defect"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"9361ea435a409883ca3d83fed76cfd2b1435fcc2e2e6b38adb7356eb62078445","item_hash_version":3,"message":"Document GH-1154 linked-test safety classification regression and canonical lineage","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
